{
  "id": "anopia",
  "term": "anopia",
  "definition": "Anopia is a loss of conscious vision in part of the visual field, such as a hemifield, leading to areas where visual perception is absent. In the packet, it refers to severe visual field loss that can be present even when standard measures of early visual pathways and visual cortex appear normal.",
